    "body": "Depends on: #64, and the F-ablation decision. The deployed R4G1 path (src/r4g1.rs) currently disables EXCT because the reference scorer quantizes counts to log-domain at probe time (float in the runtime path — contract violation). Move the quantization to compile time: store ΔX entries as ScoreQ residuals in EXCT with the standard storage descriptor, so the deployed scorer reads integers only and exact-context evidence becomes deployable. Acceptance: deployed scorer uses EXCT with zero float ops (source scan); Gate C deployed-mode (with residualized EXCT) numbers equal or beat the probe-quantized reference; witness replay covers the new entries (Theorems 6/10 intact); R4G1.md EXCT payload spec updated.\n\n\n---\n\n## Definition of Done\n- EXCT residuals are quantized at compile time into ScoreQ entries with the standard storage descriptor; the deployed scorer reads integers only.\n- The deployed path (src/r4g1.rs) re-enables exact-context evidence under the integer-only contract.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Source scan: zero float ops in the deployed EXCT read path.\n- [ ] Gate C deployed-mode (residualized EXCT) equals or beats the probe-quantized reference numbers.\n- [ ] Witness replay covers the new EXCT entries; Theorems 6/10 tests stay green.\n- [ ] `docs/transformerless/R4G1.md` EXCT payload spec updated to the residualized layout.",
